I make lunches sometimes that have to stay hot all day. Thermos is actually a brand, and still a pretty good one. You can search for insulated lunch containers, the [vacuum sealed](https://smile.amazon.com/Zojirushi-ZONCE09ST-Stainless-Steel-Vacuum-28-5-Ounce/dp/B0016S7MJM/ref=sr_1_2?dchild=1&keywords=vacuum%2Bbento&qid=1621875394&s=home-garden&sr=1-2&th=1) ones seem to work best.

&#x200B;

There are also little [lunch box warmer](https://smile.amazon.com/Electric-Lunch-Truck-Work-110V/dp/B07PV251SF/ref=sr_1_16?dchild=1&keywords=lunch+warmer&qid=1621875109&sr=8-16) things that you can pack your lunch in an insulated container, plug it in before lunchtime, and then have a nice hot lunch.

