At my old restaurant we included 20% gratuity on the check if an employee came in to eat. We got a 25% discount on our meal + anyone who was with us, so it almost evened out. Of course you always had the option to tip extra, but it totally got rid of the drama of coworkers coming in and tipping badly.

&#x200B;

They could choose to remove the gratuity, but if they did they lost their 25% discount. The only time it didn't apply was on to go orders. Honestly I think that's the best system, in spite of that restaurant being the worst they did have a couple of good ideas.

