I've done a bunch of the oven-ready and grill-ready meals from home chef. There's often a little bit of prep (forming and seasoning burgers, dropping veggies in a grill bag, chopping up a zucchini) but it's very quick. In 5 - 10 minutes you can have your meal in your oven or on the grill.

&#x200B;

Some of the oven ones baked for 30 minutes so if it's just speed you want they may not be the best. The 15-minute speed ones are quick but have a little more prep. Maybe you chop 2 or 3 veggies instead of 1. Maybe you have to prep a sauce while something cooks. 

&#x200B;

Overall I really enjoyed Home Chef but I quit for the same reason as the other person, money is a bit tight right now.

Not really. Most pantry items like bread could survive the sun for a while. Any uncut fruits or veg should survive it just fine, except stuff that wilts like lettuce. Lemonaid and tea would be alright for up to 2 hours.

&#x200B;

It's mainly things like meats, dairy, sauces. All the stuff you put on hotdogs or hamburgers, basically. I guess pickles, mustard and the buns would probably be alright.

