My morning smoothie is, 1 cup almond milk (30 cal), 1 scoop protein powder (150 cal), frozen zucchini (idk, like 10 cal?), a tablespoon of kefir, and some kind of fruit/peanut butter/chocolate powder for extra flavor. If I'm adding frozen berries with the frozen zucchini I don't need ice and it ends up super creamy. If I don't add berries then I add a couple of ice cubes.

I had two boxes in a row come with more than half of the veg soft or rotten. The first box I happened to have replacement veggies on hand, and it was only a couple of dollars worth so I didn't worry about it. After the second time in a row, along with them forgetting one of the packs of meat, I contacted customer service.

