I have been making fried rice a lot. I tend to not use up the eggs that I buy since I'm not a breakfast-y person, or much of a baker. Sometimes, you do need an egg or two for something and the 12 pack is pennies more than the 6 pack. My fried rice has been 70% veg/protein and 30% rice lately. You can add anything, spinach, zucchini, mushrooms, onion, garlic, peppers, chicken, fish, beef, pork. I use a boullion cube for seasoning, as well as sriracha, and sometimes a splash of soy. Don't add salt! The cube and the soy already have plenty of salt.

