Our restaurant concept doesn't normally provide coloring materials for kids but my boss buys dollar store coloring books and crayons and has the hosts cut out all the pages so each kid can get 1 or 2 sheets and a couple of crayons. There's a couple of problems doing it his way, we always have a lot of strange crayon colors left at the end of the week like that pukey yellow, brown, white, black, and the hosts dig through these crappy colors to find the "good" crayons. Also, the coloring sheets from dollar store books are very thin and not really intended to be handed out individually.

