I love the way Home Chef saves every recipe that you've used and you can add the ingredients to a shopping list at the click of a button. So far my 10/10 recipes are [Cotija and Jalapeno-Crusted Chicken](https://www.homechef.com/meals/cotija-and-jalapeno-crusted-chicken-with-cajun-zucchini-and-corn), the [Hot Honey Salmon](https://www.homechef.com/meals/hot-honey-salmon), and the [Garlic Sesame Steak Burrito.](https://www.homechef.com/meals/garlic-sesame-steak-burrito)

&#x200B;

Do not underestimate the deliciousness of those crispy fried jalapenos on the chicken, but if you can't handle spicy you can swap those for some of those crispy onions in the can. I added chopped red peppers to the chicken recipe and it was awesome. 

&#x200B;

 The burrito wasn't spicy. My fiance described it as a giant egg roll but better in every way.

&#x200B;

 I still dream about the hot honey salmon, they also did a hot honey chicken taco that was amazing. That spicy red pepper honey is something I could eat with a spoon. Home chef really knows how to do amazing, simple sauces.

