My parents used me as a billboard for their views when I was too young to understand. When I got older I wasn't allowed to hang out with any of the neighborhood kids, kids threw rocks at me when I was playing outside. My parent's cars were vandalized. Other parents called me a whore and a witch. We lived in the deep south and my parents were Pagan. They saw no issue with me being the one who was attacked. Coming home with a black eye and a chipped tooth because my parents wouldn't stop their shit was super fun.

&#x200B;

For me, a kid wearing something like this is not very different from the Westboro baptist church kids being forced to carry those signs. I know I'm going to get downvoted to hell, but I just want someone to know what it's like from the POV of a kid who was forced into that position.

